{
  "version": 1,
  "gg_release": "101.4",
  "comment": [
    "Pinned Nexus IDs. These are deliberately fixed rather than auto-assigned so",
    "that smali stays byte-stable across rebuilds. If a future GG release reaches",
    "this range, preflight reports a collision and they must be bumped here.",
    "",
    "gg_observed is a RECORD of what GG 101.4 used for the views Nexus binds to.",
    "It is not the source of truth: ids.gg(name) resolves by NAME from the tree's",
    "public.xml at apply time, so a weekly GG release that renumbers works",
    "automatically. The recorded hex only lets `ids` report drift.",
    "",
    "A name that DISAPPEARS is always fatal -- it means GG removed or renamed the",
    "view Nexus depends on, and silently binding to something else would be worse",
    "than failing.",
    "",
    "Strings are pinned ONLY when smali reads them with Context.getString(). A",
    "string referenced from a layout XML (the nexus_str_float_* names on the",
    "floating interface, for instance) needs no pin: aapt2 resolves @string/... by",
    "name at build time. Pinning one anyway breaks postflight, which requires",
    "every pinned string to appear as a const in smali -- add it to the xml_only",
    "set in nexus/checks.py if that is ever wanted."
  ],
